# PR and ContextStream Traceability

When creating or filling a **pull request** that implements a PRD or Tech Plan:

## 1. Populate PR description (required)

- Use [.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md](../../.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md) and fill:
  - **Summary** (what changed, why)
  - **Traceability** section with:
    - **Implements (Tech Plan):** TP-XXX IDs from [.github/traceability-mapping.yaml](../../.github/traceability-mapping.yaml)
    - **PRD:** PRD-XXX this work traces to
    - **Doc links:** Markdown links to PRD and tech plan doc(s) per the traceability mapping
    - **Labels:** Apply traceability labels from [.github/labels.yaml](../../.github/labels.yaml)
- If a feature-specific PR description doc exists (e.g. `.github/PR_DESCRIPTION_*.md`), use it to prefill Summary and Traceability; then ensure the PR body still matches the template.
- Do not skip; fill the PR description before or when opening the PR.

## 2. After PR is opened or merged — ContextStream (when MCP available)

- Capture an **implementation event** so the knowledge graph shows **PR ↔ Tech Plan ↔ PRD**:
  - Use **session(action=capture, event_type=implementation, ...)** with:
    - **title:** e.g. `PR #<number>: <short summary> (TP-XXX)`
    - **content:** `<PR URL>. Implements TP-XXX, PRD-XXX. <one-line summary>.`
    - **provenance:** `{ "pr_url": "<PR URL>" }`
    - **code_refs:** array of file paths from the traceability mapping (PRD and TP doc paths)
- See [ContextStream mapping §1.4](../../docs/guides/contextstream-mapping.md#14-linking-pull-requests-to-tech-plans-and-prds-graph-visible).

## 3. Labels (when opening the PR)

- Add GitHub labels from [.github/labels.yaml](../../.github/labels.yaml) (e.g. `prd:PRD-001`, `tech-plan:TP-SPOC-004`).
- Labels may be synced automatically when the PR body contains the Traceability section; otherwise add manually or via `gh pr edit --add-label`.

